silm:instances_papers_02_music_sections_06_closure_yoneda_hom_leg__leg_6 a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "description]\\\\ \\& \\& |[schemanode]| $(MusicEngine,-)$ tikzcd% The Yoneda closure for the Music engine: absorbed sources enter through the incoming profile \\((-,MusicEngine)\\), flow through typed nodes and olog legs via cocone maps, and exit through the outgoing profile \\((MusicEngine,-)\\). The engine is known entirely by these two profiles.fig:music-yoneda-closure theorem[Music engine Yoneda closure] thm:music-yoneda-closure The Music graph engine is completely characterized by its representable Hom-profiles: \\[ MusicEngine ( (-,MusicEngine), (MusicEngine,-) ). \\] Specifically: enumerate Every absorbed source, typed witness, manifest, schema, and Mittens source leg enters through an arrow \\(f:X\\) in the incoming profile. Every admitted task, rendered section, catalog trace, and forbidden-path report exits through an arrow \\(g:MusicEngine Y\\) in the outgoing profile. enumerate theorem proof Step 1 (symbols). \\((-,MusicEngine)\\) is the incoming Yoneda profile, collecting all morphisms into the engine. \\((MusicEngine,-)\\) is the outgoing Yoneda profile, collecting all morphisms out. Step 2 (operation). Yoneda's lemma says that natural transformations \\((-,A)(-,B)\\) correspond bijectively to morphisms \\(A B\\) in \\(\\). Step 3 (base topic). Yoneda's lemma and the representable functor discipline. Step 4 (concrete anchor). The Mittens body-mass observation enters as \\(f:MittensBodyMassRecord\\) in the incoming profile. The rendered quality section exits as \\(g:MusicEngine\\) in the outgoing profile. Step 5 (Yoneda traversal). The Yoneda embedding \\(Y:[op,]\\) is fully faithful, so \\(MusicEngine\\) is determined up to isomorphism by its representable. Step 6 (recap). The Music engine is closed when both profiles are fully populated and their composition laws commute. proof Diagram law (Figure~fig:music-yoneda-closure): incoming and outgoing profiles are not optional metadata; they are the Yoneda characterization of the engine as a category-theoretic object. An engine with empty profiles is an engine that cannot be known. [0.88]% tikzcd[column sep=large,row sep=large,ampersand replacement=\\&] |[schemanode]| IncomingProfile [r," .
